# Generated by `npm run generate-types` (cf-content-types-generator), which does
# not run Prettier. Formatting them here only means the next regeneration
# reverts it and the drift comes straight back — and then someone reformats them
# into an unrelated PR, which is the exact problem this check exists to stop.
src/app/generated-types/

# Generated by `npm run export-content`. Same reasoning, and it is a 5 MB
# machine-written file nobody reads.
src/contentful-types/

# LEGAL DOCUMENTS. Deliberately not style-managed.
#
# These are the privacy policy, terms of use, accessibility declaration and
# Liquidity Hub terms, in three languages. A lawyer or an editor replaces them
# wholesale; nobody edits them line by line. Prettier would rewrap paragraphs
# and normalise list markers, which produces a diff on a legal document that
# nobody asked for and that obscures the one time somebody DOES change a clause.
src/content/legal/

# FAQ documents, same treatment for the same reason.
src/content/faq/

# Legacy author markdown copied verbatim from the old Cuttlebelle site, used as
# input by the migration scripts. Source data we did not write and do not edit.
scripts/orbs-website-migration/authors/

# Build output, dependencies and review artefacts.
.next/
node_modules/
storybook-static/
.visual/
coverage/
